const faq = [
  { q: 'What is the Old Norse word for raven?', a: 'The Old Norse word for raven is hrafn (masculine noun). The plural is hrafnar. It is the standard word for the Common Raven (Corvus corax) in Old Norse texts, place names, and personal names. The word is cognate with Old English hræfn and modern German Rabe.' },
  { q: 'How do you pronounce hrafn in Old Norse?', a: 'Old Norse pronunciation: "HRAHVN" (the h is aspirated before r, so the initial sound is like a strongly breathed-out H followed by R). The vowel is short, and the final -n is a sonorant. Modern Icelandic preserves this as "HRAPBN" (approximate). Many English speakers use a simplified "RAHN" or "HRAVN".' },
  { q: 'What is the modern Icelandic word for raven?', a: 'Modern Icelandic retains hrafn (singular) and hrafnar (plural), very close to the Old Norse form. Modern Norwegian uses ravn, Swedish uses korp, Danish uses ravn. All are descended from the same Proto-Germanic root.' },
];
---

